This PR updates the frontend tests to use the updated `userEvent` API, introduce consistency in the test files, and cleans them of any unused artifacts. I have also removed the old and now unused `useTyping` hook and fixed/passed a formerly skipped test.

---

**Give a summary of what the PR does, explaining any non-trivial design decisions**
All files have been modified in one or more of the following ways:

- Consistent usage of the test queries from the `screen` constant (`@testing-library/react`) rather than from the test render return. This is more flexible as it allows the developer to update the used query quickly, and is also a common standard.

**Before**
```tsx
const { getByText } = render(<SomeComponent />);
const button = getByText("Close");
```

**After**
```tsx
import { screen } from "@testing-library/react";

render(<SomeComponent />);
const button = screen.getByText("Close");
```

- Proper utilization of the v14 `userEvent` API. Primarily, this omits the requirement of wrapping the test actions with an `act` since the new version handles this internally. I have also replaced any test files that utilize the `fireEvent` API with `userEvent`. This simulates more realistic user events (read more about this [here](https://testing-library.com/docs/user-event/intro#differences-from-fireevent)).

**Before**
```tsx
const button = getByText("Close");

await act(async () => {
  await userEvent.click(button);
});
```

**After**
```tsx
const user = userEvent.setup();
const button = getByText("Close");

await user.click(button);
```

- Refactored/proper mock definitions
